e row is taller than the last. Atlas floats in the sky and hops.","cast":[{"actor":"atlas","do":"slide","instant":true,"at":{"x":26,"y":9}},{"actor":"maya","do":"enter","walk":true,"from":{"x":-14,"y":26},"at":{"x":15,"y":26},"ms":1200},{"actor":"atlas","do":"play","at":{"x":26,"y":9},"atMs":1400}]},{"frame":"stacks","caption":"Lesson 1: Maya's gains earned gains. Interest, the extra paid for using your money, can earn interest too: compound interest.","a11y":"Maya beside four stacks of gold coins, each taller than the last by more: lesson 1's gains growing too. Atlas floats above and blinks.","cast":[{"actor":"atlas","do":"slide","instant":true,"at":{"x":52,"y":14}},{"actor":"atlas","do":"play","at":{"x":52,"y":14},"atMs":600}]},{"frame":"ground","caption":"Say Maya's $100 grows 8% a year, every gain left in. Atlas asks: how many years until it doubles to $200?","a11y":"Maya on the orchard ground beside one gold coin, her 100 dollars. A dashed outline twice as tall appears beside it. Atlas hops.","cast":[{"actor":"maya","do":"slide","instant":true,"at":{"x":8,"y":26}},{"actor":"atlas","do":"slide","instant":true,"at":{"x":48,"y":16}},{"actor":"now-1","do":"enter","at":{"x":27,"y":45},"atMs":300,"ms":400},{"actor":"target","do":"enter","at":{"x":36,"y":43},"atMs":900,"ms":400},{"actor":"atlas","do":"play","at":{"x":48,"y":16},"atMs":1500}]}]},"toggle":{"kind":"toggle","title":"The rule of 72","artKey":"if3","footer":"Example: $100 growing 8% a year, every gain left in. Real growth swings.","states":[{"chip":"9 years","frame":"ground","caption":"Quick guess: divide 72 by the percent it grows each year. 72 ÷ 8 = 9. It doubles every 9 years.","a11y":"Maya's one gold coin, and beside it a stack of two coins: her money 9 years on, about twice as much.","labels":[{"id":"total","text":"About $200","at":{"x":44,"y":40},"tone":"accent"}],"cast":[{"actor":"maya","do":"slide","instant":true,"at":{"x":8,"y":26}},{"actor":"now-1","do":"enter","at":{"x":27,"y":45},"atMs":300,"ms":400},{"actor":"now-2","do":"enter","at":{"x":36,"y":43},"atMs":300,"ms":400}]},{"chip":"36 years","frame":"ground","caption":"It keeps doubling every 9 years. The last 9 years alone added about $800, more than the 27 years before.","a11y":"Five stacks in a row, one every 9 years: 1 coin, 2, 4, 8, then 16. Each stack is twice as tall as the one before.","labels":[{"id":"total","text":"About $1,600","at":{"x":31,"y":15},"tone":"accent"}],"cast":[{"actor":"maya","do":"slide","instant":true,"at":{"x":8,"y":26}},{"actor":"now-1","do":"enter","at":{"x":27,"y":45},"atMs":300,"ms":400},{"actor":"now-2","do":"enter","at":{"x":36,"y":43},"atMs":300,"ms":400},{"actor":"now-4","do":"enter","at":{"x":45,"y":39},"atMs":500,"ms":400},{"actor":"now-8","do":"enter","at":{"x":54,"y":31},"atMs":700,"ms":400},{"actor":"now-16","do":"enter","at":{"x":63,"y":15},"atMs":900,"ms":400}]},{"chip":"Wait 9 years","frame":"ground","caption":"Say she waits 9 years to start. 36 years from now, she has one doubling fewer: half as much.","a11y":"The same row starts one step later: 1 coin, 2, 4, then 8. A dashed outline above the 8 shows the 16 coins she would have had.","labels":[{"id":"total","text":"About $800","at":{"x":32,"y":30},"tone":"warn"}],"cast":[{"actor":"maya","do":"slide","instant":true,"at":{"x":8,"y":26}},{"actor":"late-1","do":"enter","at":{"x":36,"y":45},"atMs":300,"ms":400},{"actor":"late-2","do":"enter","at":{"x":45,"y":43},"atMs":450,"ms":400},{"actor":"late-4","do":"enter","at":{"x":54,"y":39},"atMs":600,"ms":400},{"actor":"late-8","do":"enter","at":{"x":63,"y":15},"atMs":750,"ms":400}]}]},"idea":{"title":"Three things decide the total","body":"How much you put in, the percent it grows each year, and how many years it grows.","explain":"In the example, only the years changed when Maya waited, and she ended with half as much.","still":"doublings"},"takeaway":{"body":"Money put in sooner has more time to grow. Here, 9 years sooner meant twice as much.","explain":"Starting later cost Maya her last doubling, the biggest one.","still":"sooner"}}
